# ======================================================================
# PRETTIER IGNORE — the whole repository
# ======================================================================
# This project's formatting is deliberate. Prettier reflowed files in ways
# that fought the existing layout and produced noisy diffs, so nothing here
# is formatted automatically.
#
# The first line ignores every path. The negations that would normally
# follow are intentionally absent: there is no opt-back-in, because no file
# in this repository should be reformatted automatically.
#
# `prettier --check .` will now report that there are no matching files
# rather than listing violations, and `prettier --write .` becomes a no-op.
# Running Prettier on an explicitly named path still works, so this stops
# automatic reformatting without removing the tool.
#
# To let Prettier format something again, add a negation below, e.g.:
#   !some/new/file.js
# ======================================================================

# Everything.
*
**/*

# Named explicitly as well, so the intent survives if the globs above are
# ever narrowed.
index.html
frequently-asked-questions.html
assets/
assets/scripts/
assets/styles/
assets/images/
mockups/
.github/
*.md
*.html
*.css
*.js
*.json
